    <categoryEntry name="Officer" id="6f24-1326-b08a-81bc" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Voice of Command" id="6212-14d3-3e2c-521f" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">During each Battle Round, this OFFICER can issue Orders to units within it&apos;s VOX RANGE.
Each OFFICER’s datasheet will specify how many Orders it can issue and which units are eligible to receive those Orders.
Unless otherwise stated, when an OFFICER issues an Order, you must select one of the Orders it knows. This can be an Order that was already issued by another OFFICER this turn, but the same OFFICER cannot attempt to issue the same Order more than once in the same phase.
Unless otherwise stated, a unit can only be given one Order of each type, each phase (any Order of the same type subsequently issued to that unit replaces the current one).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Astra Militarum Auxilia" id="c93e-e4e5-1298-204c" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Auxilia Vox Range" id="1164-8c51-cd2e-50b9" hidden="true" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <comment>Infantry</comment>
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">This unit is considered to be in VOX RANGE of an OFFICER unit if:
- Is within 6&quot; of that OFFICER unit.
- Is within 6&quot; of an INFANTRY unit already in VOX RANGE and within 12&quot; of that OFFICER squad.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="or">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="3d52-fccf-10c0-3fae" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                    <condition childId="3d52-fccf-10c0-3fae" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Navis Imperialis" id="5148-4ab3-b792-38fe" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Death from Above" id="c937-0ff6-df66-59fe" hidden="true" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">During deployment, if every model in this unit has this ability, then you can set up this unit high in the skies instead of setting it up on the battlefield. If you do, then in the Reinforcements step of one of your Movement phases you can set up this unit anywhere on the battlefield that is more than D3+6&quot; away from enemy models.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
          <modifiers>
            <modifier field="hidden" type="set" value="false">
              <conditionGroups>
                <conditionGroup type="and">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition childId="3d52-fccf-10c0-3fae" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="ancestor" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                        <condition childId="3d52-fccf-10c0-3fae" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="instanceOf" value="0"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                  <conditions>
                    <condition childId="901d-9cf4-c32e-cdbf" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="true" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="equalTo" value="1"/>
                  </conditions>
                </conditionGroup>
              </conditionGroups>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Faction: Adeptus Arbites" id="ffb2-0540-4815-57ea" hidden="false"/>
    <categoryEntry name="Chaotic Astartes" id="62d9-3cd6-aed7-34fe" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Wanton acts" id="1cf9-2227-447e-5320" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Each time a model with this ability makes an attack against an enemy unit within 12&quot; with any weapon type except Bomb, Tactical or the attack is affected by Indirect Fire rule, an unmodified hit roll of 6 scores 1 additional hit.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Malicious Volleys" id="5574-1566-dddd-9675" hidden="false">
          <description>Instead of following the normal rules for Rapid Fire weapons,  models in this unit shooting Rapid Fire bolt weapons make double the number of attacks if any of the following apply:
- The shooting model’s target is within half the weapon’s range.
- The shooting model is INFANTRY and its unit Remained Stationary in your previous Movement phase.
- The shooting model is a TERMINATOR.
For the purposes of this ability, a Rapid Fire bolt weapon is any bolt weapon with the Rapid Fire type.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Dark Priest" id="9179-1ae8-54eb-1abd" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Demagogue [Aura]" id="16fd-a031-e1b7-d89a" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">While a friendly &lt;LEGION&gt; CORE, &lt;LEGION&gt; DAEMONKIN or &lt;LEGION&gt; CULTISTS unit is within 6&quot; of this model, models in that unit can use this model’s Leadership characteristic instead of their own.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Priest" id="ee51-f7b1-2194-c061" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">This unit’s PRIEST model knows Dark Zealotry and one other prayer from the Prayers to the Dark Gods. 
In your Command phase, this unit’s PRIEST model can attempt to chant one prayer it knows that has not already been attempted by a friendly model this turn. Roll one D6: on a 3+, the prayer is heard and takes effect until the start of your next Command phase. Each time a prayer chanted by this unit’s PRIEST model is heard, measure distances and draw line of sight from that PRIEST model.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Priest" id="bb4e-2765-fb54-3ad5" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Emboldened by Prayer [Aura]" id="0843-510f-9a27-c3d6" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">While a friendly REGIMENT INFANTRY or IMPERIUM SERVANT CORE unit is within 6&quot; of this model, models in that unit can use this model’s Leadership characteristic instead of their own.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Priest" id="dca5-16df-b2b6-f2e1" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">This model knows War Hymn and one other hymn from the Hymns of Battle. In your Command phase, if this model is on the battlefield, it can intone one hymn it knows that has not already been intoned by a friendly model this turn. Roll one D6: on a 3+, the intoned hymn is inspiring and takes effect until the start of your next Command phase.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
    <categoryEntry name="Dumb weapon" id="e2fa-b062-134a-0604" hidden="false">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Dumb weapon" id="d36c-1d4d-c574-9bbb" hidden="false" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">Instead of following the normal rules of a Tactical Weapon, in your next Shooting phase, you can only let the attack to be executed in the selected point, affecting each unit within the range indicated in the weapon&apos;s datasheet.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </categoryEntry>
